Constructor variant of cpp17_template_arg_completed_later: the stale
incomplete-base instance reaches symex and aborts an invariant in
symex_assign (SIGABRT) rather than erroring in the front end.
Investigated 2026-07-28: a staleness-remark mechanism
(#had_incomplete_arg on the instance, re-elaboration at the later
point of instantiation) re-runs the instantiation but the re-run
never rebuilds the BASE list (bases()=0 across all elaborations): the
template's stored declaration loses the base-clause information after
the first instantiation, so re-elaboration needs the body/base-clause
preserved first.  Deeper than the cache policy.
Round-6 note (2026-08-02): see the companion test's parked findings;
additionally this variant's get() body (return *this) needs the
derived-to-private-base conversion once the layout root is fixed.
Round-9 update: the layout root is FIXED (companion test CORE); this
variant is now non-vacuous and no longer aborts symex, but the
explicit constructor still converts to an EMPTY body at the rebuild
(the mem-initializer via the template parameter is dropped even with
the map-first matching) -- one residual conversion-ordering layer.
Fixed 2026-08-04 (round 10): the re-instantiation reset now really
erases the stale members (angle-aware "tag-" strip; the drain queue is
purged before the removal), so the rebuilt constructor converts with
its base mem-initializer intact.
